        {
          "title": "Query Pipeline and Optimizer Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Pipeline and Declarative SQL",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Parse",
                    "sub": "syntax, parse tree",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Bind",
                    "sub": "tables, types, permissions",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Rewrite",
                    "sub": "views, subqueries, constants",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Plan",
                    "sub": "pick cheapest",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Execute",
                    "sub": "return rows",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "SQL is ==declarative==: you say what, the optimizer picks how",
                "Same query, {orange:different plan} as data changes"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Rewrite vs Plan",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Rewrite",
                "Planner"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Basis",
                  "Fixed rules, no costing",
                  "Cost estimates"
                ],
                [
                  "Does",
                  "Expand views, flatten IN/EXISTS, fold constants, push predicates down",
                  "Picks access paths, join order, join methods"
                ],
                [
                  "Result",
                  "Same query, simpler",
                  "Cheapest estimate, not guaranteed fastest"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Cached Plans",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Selectivity== = fraction of rows a value matches",
                "Plan cached for a {red:rare} value stays slow for a {green:common} one",
                "SQL Server: sniffing; PostgreSQL: generic plan",
                "PostgreSQL: 5 custom plans first, then generic if not costlier"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "PREPARE q(text) AS SELECT * FROM orders WHERE status = $1;",
                "SET plan_cache_mode = force_generic_plan;",
                "EXECUTE q('rare');",
                "EXECUTE q('common'); -- same plan"
              ],
              "note": "forces one reused plan"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Optimizer picks the cheapest **estimated** plan; bad estimates mean bad plans"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Cost-Based Optimization, Statistics and Selectivity",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Cost-Based Optimization, Statistics and Selectivity",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Cost and Statistics",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Cost = ==I/O + CPU== estimate in abstract units, not ms",
                "PostgreSQL: `seq_page_cost`=1.0, `random_page_cost`=4.0",
                "`ANALYZE` / `UPDATE STATISTICS` stores row and page count",
                "Per column: distinct count, null fraction",
                "Most common values + frequencies, histogram buckets"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Selectivity",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Selectivity = ==fraction of rows kept== (0 to 1)",
                "Estimated rows = table rows × selectivity",
                "Equality ≈ `1 / distinct values`, unless in the most-common list",
                "AND multiplies: sel(A) × sel(B)"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Case",
                "Calc",
                "Rows"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "50 distinct, 100,000 rows",
                  "1/50 × 100,000",
                  "2,000"
                ],
                [
                  "A 0.1 AND B 0.1",
                  "0.1 × 0.1",
                  "1% of table"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. When Estimates Break",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Correlated columns (city, zip): {red:underestimates} by orders of magnitude",
                "Stale statistics or skewed data: wrong row counts",
                "Early error compounds into wrong join order and method"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Fix the estimate",
              "text": "==ANALYZE==, then extended (multi-column) statistics, or a higher statistics target."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Index Scans vs Sequential Scans",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Index Scans vs Sequential Scans",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Choosing a Scan",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Scan",
                "Reads",
                "Wins when"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Seq",
                  "every page, in order",
                  "most of the table"
                ],
                [
                  "Index",
                  "B-tree, then heap rows (random I/O)",
                  "few rows"
                ],
                [
                  "Index-only",
                  "index alone, if pages all-visible",
                  "covering index"
                ],
                [
                  "Bitmap",
                  "page bitmap, heap in physical order",
                  "medium; AND/OR of indexes"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Index wins under ==5-10%== of rows",
                "Above that a ==seq scan== is cheaper: the planner is right",
                "Index-only needs the {green:visibility map} (vacuumed table)"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Why the Index Is Skipped",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Function or cast on the column: `lower(email)=...`",
                "Leading wildcard: `LIKE '%x'`",
                "Type mismatch, or a ==tiny table==",
                "Wrong column order in a composite index"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "CREATE INDEX ON users (lower(email));",
                "CREATE INDEX ON orders (cust_id) INCLUDE (total);"
              ],
              "note": "expression index; covering index"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Composite and Covering",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Composite `(a,b)` serves `a` and `a+b`, ==not b alone==",
                "`INCLUDE` columns enable an ==index-only scan==",
                "Low-cardinality columns rarely benefit"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Seq scan is not a bug",
              "text": "When most rows match, a ==seq scan== beats the index. Trust the planner."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
